 a  lot of confidence in this team we have a  lot of confidence in the players and  what we can do uh so we're just gonna  come in and hold each other accountable  put a great week of practice  in the books and move forward and worry  about getting a win on sunday we just  know our best balls ahead of us  what more deck do you personally have to  do to get the offense to where you think  it needs to be  yeah just focus on the details of the  whole offense um not with just within my  game but just with the whole offense uh  taking the little things and focusing  those because those little things uh  come back and can beat you or hurt you  uh when you're playing these good teams  and when you're playing games that  matter so  for me it's just going to be about being  the general of that and making sure that  we're focusing on the small things and  the details and the nuances of our  offense and i know the big plays and  everything will come  you referred to kellen moore earlier as  a genius give me a specific example of  something he's done or said that's  caused you to say wow this guy's got it  yeah i mean he's got a good timing a  good timing with his plays  the way he sees the defense the way he  studies  the opponent's coordinator and the  things that they're doing um there's  been a few times whether it's at  practice or maybe just in a game i'm  thinking of a certain play uh because  we've discussed we've discussed it or  whatever and we've discussed a certain  situation and boom he calls it and it  leads to a touchdown so there's a lot of  examples but it's just his timing the  way he sees the game  when you are missing offensive linemen  like tyron smith going into last week's  game lyle collins during the game how  does that affect your role and your job  on a play-in and play out basis  yeah you know i mean it really can't and  that's the tough part that's the tough  part about our job and tough part about  football is you can't allow  something like that bother you or get it  with your mind uh but what allows  our offense and allows me to have that  trust is we we've got some good guys  that that can play we've got some good  guys that are are playing  uh in place of tyron smith and lyle  collins so if you go back and look at it  uh just knowing about trusting those  guys they're going to do whatever it  takes to get the job done cam flim is a  fighter i trust you many day of the week  on my backside and we had a couple we  had a good young briggy come in  on the right side and brandon knight who  pointed tell off on the back end of it  so just focus on  just making sure those guys are  confident in themselves and knowing that  hey  i'm not worried about it i know you're  going to get the job done  jason whitton is back after one year in  broadcasting what's the biggest change  you've noticed in him  i had nothing changed nothing changed at  all i mean jason  approached pro on and off the field  somebody i've always  looked up to and watched everything that  he'd done he sets the standard so  when jason came back um it was great and  then i mean it was it was great for this  team  in the locker room on the field and then  outside of that what he just means to  guys and the leader he is  so i mean  it was great for us  now if i were to ask him that same  question about you how has dak prescott  changed in the year that you were gone  jason what and what do you think he  would say  yeah i'm not too sure maybe just a  little bit of  maybe being more vocal as a leader i  don't know i've always felt like i was  vocal  um  i don't know i've gotten better i want  to say in every aspect of the game i  mean i put a lot of time and focus in  doing that so i would hope you would say  that but we've got to ask him  well one way you've changed dak and this  is changing all the time you have more  and more off-field partnerships and  today it's directv now i've got a direct  tv hookup down in my barn i had the game  in 4k last thu